<article class="env-definition" id="02XN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02XN">Definition <span data-tag="02XN">4.33.6</span>.</a> Assume $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ is a fibred category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>choice of pullbacks</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000019196" id="a0000019196-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> for $p : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{C}$ is given by a choice of a strongly cartesian morphism $f^\ast x \to x$ lying over $f$ for any morphism $f: V \to U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ and any $x \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{S}_ U)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Given a choice of pullbacks, for any morphism $f : V \to U$ of $\mathcal{C}$ the functor $f^* : \mathcal{S}_ U \to \mathcal{S}_ V$ described above is called a <em>pullback functor</em> (associated to the choices $f^*x \to x$ made above). 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>